1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,728
Overpay the mortgage,

2
00:00:01,728 --> 00:00:02,431
or invest?

3
00:00:02,431 --> 00:00:04,542
Sort these three things first.

4
00:00:04,542 --> 00:00:04,824
One:

5
00:00:04,824 --> 00:00:06,090
an emergency fund.

6
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:07,779
Overpaid money is locked

7
00:00:07,779 --> 00:00:08,835
into the house,

8
00:00:08,835 --> 00:00:10,664
and it's hard to get back.

9
00:00:10,664 --> 00:00:10,946
Two:

10
00:00:10,946 --> 00:00:14,253
if your employer matches pension contributions,

11
00:00:14,253 --> 00:00:15,660
take the full match.

12
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,138
Fifty pounds from you

13
00:00:17,138 --> 00:00:18,615
can become a hundred.

14
00:00:18,615 --> 00:00:19,038
Three:

15
00:00:19,038 --> 00:00:20,515
clear debts that cost

16
00:00:20,515 --> 00:00:22,204
more than your mortgage,

17
00:00:22,204 --> 00:00:23,471
like credit cards.

18
00:00:23,471 --> 00:00:25,300
Then compare your mortgage

19
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,778
rate with a realistic

20
00:00:26,778 --> 00:00:28,044
return after fees.
